From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 05:34:25 +0000
Subject: build: pass the repack allowlist relative to the build dir

repack() passes --allowlist through rebase_path() without a base
directory, which gives a system-absolute path, so the command line of
every repack step with an allowlist embeds the absolute path of the
checkout and output directory. That makes the step impossible to run on
a remote worker, whose checkout lives elsewhere, and puts the local path
into its cache key, so no two checkouts ever share a cache hit for it.

Rebase it against root_build_dir like the other arguments. Actions run
with the build dir as their working directory, so pak_util.py opens the
same file.

This should be upstreamed. Drop this patch once upstream
tools/grit/repack.gni passes repack_allowlist through
rebase_path(..., root_build_dir); check that line on each Chromium roll.

diff --git a/tools/grit/repack.gni b/tools/grit/repack.gni
index fff9c32e154cf76096878cf574b84b8d301a68df..b27e4d8e1c4979bbbe2f90c80a5577b8036f2aa6 100644
--- a/tools/grit/repack.gni
+++ b/tools/grit/repack.gni
@@ -76,7 +76,7 @@ template("repack") {
     args = [ "repack" ]
     if (defined(invoker.repack_allowlist)) {
       inputs += [ invoker.repack_allowlist ]
-      _rebased_allowlist = rebase_path(invoker.repack_allowlist)
+      _rebased_allowlist = rebase_path(invoker.repack_allowlist, root_build_dir)
       args += [ "--allowlist=$_rebased_allowlist" ]
       args += [ "--suppress-removed-key-output" ]
     }
